# Cargo: check, build, and run

Package root is `hello_cargo/` (not the workspace root). There is no default binary.

## How to invoke (required)

Always use one of these exact forms — do not rely on a shell working_directory alone:

- `cd hello_cargo && cargo run --bin <name>`
- `cargo run --manifest-path hello_cargo/Cargo.toml --bin <name>`

Same for `check` / `build`. Never run bare `cargo …` from the workspace root.

## check vs build vs run

- Prefer `cargo check` for fast verification (no executable).
- Use `cargo build` or `cargo run --bin <name>` when an executable is needed.
- Always pass `--bin hello_1` or `--bin hello_2` (or another bin name when added).
- Use `--release` only when asked or when measuring performance.
- To debug with a breakpoint: `cd hello_cargo && cargo build --bin <name>`, then `lldb -b -o "breakpoint set --file <name>.rs --line <n>" -o run -o bt -o continue ./target/debug/<name>`.
